# Python bytecode. `.github/scripts/` is run by CI and by hand, and a stray
# `__pycache__` was committed by a `git add -A` -- in front of the gate that
# fails the build on any generated file left in the tree. A `.pyc` records the
# source's mtime, so a fresh checkout regenerates it and the gate reports a
# drift that is entirely its own.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# JVM crash artefacts. A heap dump is large and can contain anything that
# was in memory, so it must never be committed by an `add -A`.
*.hprof
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
.kotlin/
